---
import CourseLayout from "../../layouts/CourseLayout.astro";
import {demonstrations} from "../../data/demonstrations";
import {withBase} from "astro-theme-university/url";
import "../../styles/demonstration.css";
---
<CourseLayout title="See it. Try it. Make it yours." description="Sixteen complete worked examples. Follow the coach through a different scenario, inspect the reasoning, then take control of the same 3D apparatus." eyebrow="THE DEMONSTRATION STUDIO" wide>
<p>These examples support preparation for in-person labs and the equivalent online route. Watch the reasoning before class, revisit it for revision, or take control when practising online. Follow your assigned brief for the campus task and required submission.</p><section class="demo-library-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">TWO WAYS INTO THE SAME EXPERIENCE</p><h2>A front-row seat.<br/>Or your hands on the controls.</h2><p>Watch a complete demonstration with chapter controls, adjustable pace, readable captions and a complete transcript. Switch to practice to test predictions, manipulate conditions and get feedback based on your own attempts.</p></div><div><h3>What a complete answer looks like</h3><p>Every example includes its finished evidence, explanation and limitations. Assessment demonstrations use different settings and data from your assigned work. They show how to learn and communicate a method.</p><a class="button primary" href={withBase("/demonstrations/assessment-final/")}>Watch Operation Lamplight ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="callout"><h2>How to use an example</h2><ol><li><strong>Choose a lab or assessment below.</strong> Read its different scenario and learning goal.</li><li><strong>Select Watch.</strong> Follow the chapters, pause, replay or change the pace. The transcript is available if you prefer reading.</li><li><strong>Select Take Control.</strong> Try the chapter's decision, then Test my decision. Use feedback and hints to understand why it works.</li><li><strong>Read the finished work.</strong> Inspect the example record and explanation, then follow the link back to your assigned lab or assessment.</li></ol><p>Your attempts here last for this visit. They do not complete the assigned activity or enter your skills passport. You can watch the entire example or take over whenever you want.</p></section>
{[["lab","TWELVE CAPABILITIES","The lab series."],["assessment","BRING THE SKILLS TOGETHER","Worked assessment projects."]].map(([kind,label,title])=><section><p class="eyebrow">{label}</p><h2>{title}</h2><div class="demo-library">{demonstrations.filter(d=>d.kind===kind).map(d=><article><span class="demo-library-number">{d.week?String(d.week).padStart(2,"0"):"EX"}</span><div><p class="eyebrow">{d.skill}</p><h3><a href={withBase("/demonstrations/"+d.id+"/")}>{d.title}</a></h3><p>{d.subtitle}</p><p class="small">{d.steps.length} chapters · {d.estimatedMinutes} minutes · 3D walkthrough + hands-on practice</p><a href={withBase("/demonstrations/"+d.id+"/")}>Open the worked example →</a></div></article>)}</div></section>)}
</CourseLayout>
